import json, pathlib, html
from datetime import date
root=pathlib.Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]
esc=html.escape
data=json.loads((root/'data/adoptions.json').read_text())
p=data['projects']
audit_date=date.fromisoformat(data['auditDate'])
audit_label=audit_date.strftime('%d %B %Y').lstrip('0')
reuse=[r for r in p if r.get('verified') and r.get('external') and r.get('countedAsReuse')]
counts={category:sum(r['category']==category for r in reuse) for category in ('Evaluation use','Software integration','Methodological adaptation')}
mentions=sum(r.get('verified') and r.get('external') and r['category']=='Citation or mention' for r in p)
preprints=sum(bool(r.get('researchPreprint')) for r in reuse if r['category']=='Evaluation use')
def counted(n, singular, plural=None):
 return f"{n} {singular if n==1 else (plural or singular+'s')}"
intro=f'''<a class="text-link" href="index.html">← Back to In the Wild</a><p class="eyebrow">RESEARCH AUDIT · {esc(audit_label.upper())}</p><h1>Every connection,<br>with its context.</h1><p>This audit identifies <b>{len(reuse)} external projects with verified reuse relationships</b>: {counted(counts['Evaluation use'], 'reported evaluation')}, {counted(counts['Software integration'], 'software integration')}, and {counted(counts['Methodological adaptation'], 'documented methodological adaptation')}. {mentions} additional projects contain verified mentions, without verified execution or integration. {preprints} of the evaluation projects have arXiv preprints. These categories overlap with artifact types; do not add the preprint count to the reuse total.</p><p>“External” means outside the dataset creators’ own projects. It does not mean the evaluation was independently replicated, that its authors were independent of the evaluated system, or that benchmark exposure was absent during development.</p><h2>What was searched and read</h2><p>Searches used ASQ-PHI, ASQ_PHI, asq_phi, the dataset DOI, and the article DOI, followed by named-project and repository-specific searches. Search-engine results supplied discovery leads; a primary source had to support each included relationship. The audit reviewed the three available scholarly full texts, their methods, results, references and available appendices, including the 64-page MedDeID PDF appendix. Bao’s initial version was checked for appearance history and v5 was read for current results. The associated software documentation, evaluation records, loaders and model/dataset cards were read as relevant to ASQ-PHI.</p><table><thead><tr><th>Surface</th><th>Coverage and limits</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Google Scholar</td><td>Direct access attempted twice; HTTP 403. Search-engine discovery used as a supplement. Complete Scholar coverage cannot be claimed.</td></tr><tr><td>arXiv</td><td>Three full papers verified: Bao 2608.03172 (latest v5), Hellemans 2609.10049 (v1), AegisVox 2610.14643 (v1). No peer-reviewed follow-up venue verified.</td></tr><tr><td>Crossref / OpenAlex / Semantic Scholar</td><td>Live article records inspected. Crossref and OpenAlex returned zero indexed citations; Semantic Scholar returned two (Bao and AegisVox). Incomplete, disagreeing index snapshots are not an adoption count.</td></tr><tr><td>GitHub</td><td>Connected code search and repository tree/source/history inspection found loaders, evaluation records and mentions. Unauthenticated code API search required authentication; connected search supplied matches. Search results are bounded, not a guarantee of all public code.</td></tr><tr><td>Hugging Face / PyPI</td><td>ASQ-PHI model/dataset queries, full relevant cards, model-family metadata, Outis package documentation, and source repositories inspected. Weight formats, mirrors, cards and package distributions were deduplicated.</td></tr><tr><td>Company and general web</td><td>Protostar validation page and Custodian artifacts inspected. Secondary summaries were used as leads, not primary proof. Public reporting does not establish customer use or clinical deployment.</td></tr></tbody></table><h2>How a connection becomes a record</h2><ol><li>Locate a public source naming the dataset or providing a dataset-specific implementation.</li><li>Read the context to distinguish a completed evaluation, an implementation path, documented methodological adaptation, and a citation or mention.</li><li>Record the source location, methods, version, limitations, and the evidence for its date.</li><li>Group related papers, packages, model cards and repositories under one project. Recheck a changed claim against the owning source.</li><li>Count only supported external evaluation, integration and methodological-adaptation relationships as reuse. Keep mention-only entries visible but outside reuse totals.</li></ol><h2>How to read the growth curve</h2><p>The curve counts source-dated external reuse projects, once per project. Dates may be an arXiv submission, an artifact commit, or an explicitly dated page update. They are <b>documented appearances, not proven first-use dates</b>. A page updated in July may describe work done earlier. No date is back-calculated from a crawler timestamp. The origin release (Mendeley v1, November 21, 2025) and original article (online February 11, 2026; April issue) appear only as timeline context. They are not external adoption.</p><h2>Material findings and scoring caveats</h2><ul><li><b>Bao / Guardian Layer:</b> earlier span-alignment and statistics were corrected. The current record uses v5. Detectability after substitution is a limited proxy, and does not establish end-to-end privacy or clinical utility.</li><li><b>MedDeID:</b> character recall and character over-redaction differ from exact entity or query-level metrics. The age-exclusion sensitivity changes what is counted as unwanted redaction.</li><li><b>AegisVox:</b> the primary contract-intersection score excludes some ASQ-PHI categories. Full-ontology results must accompany it. The ASQ experiment concerns text detection, not the audio system’s end-to-end privacy.</li><li><b>Outis and Inkguard:</b> development exposure and tuning splits matter. External authorship does not make every evaluation an untouched held-out test.</li><li><b>HANK and Protostar:</b> implementation/annotation policies differ, and some comparison baselines are quoted rather than rerun. Protostar reports recall in differing contexts; this audit does not merge them into a single score.</li><li><b>All projects:</b> no results were independently rerun in this audit. Synthetic benchmark performance does not demonstrate real patient-note performance, HIPAA compliance, certification, clinical safety, endorsement, or production deployment.</li></ul><h2>Deduplication and exclusions</h2><p>Bao’s paper, Guardian Layer code, reproducibility site and slides are one project. MedDeID’s paper and associated model/repositories are one project. HANK weight formats and related cards are one family. Outis’s PyPI, GitHub and model artifacts are one project. The Korean dataset’s associated downstream model is not counted as a second ASQ-PHI user.</p><p>Creator-owned SafeSearch, the original article/repository/data deposit, AMIA dissemination, secondary news or summaries, and a repository fork without verified downstream use are excluded from external reuse counts. Clinical GLiNER KG and EuroPriv-Bench remain mention-only. The audit found no basis to claim all listed models were trained on ASQ-PHI. Unverified private use is unknown.</p><h2>Project evidence index</h2>'''
parts=[]
for r in p:
 links=' · '.join(f'<a href="{esc(s["url"],quote=True)}">{esc(s["label"])} ↗</a>' for s in r['sources'])
 parts.append(f'<article id="{esc(r["id"])}"><h2>{esc(r["name"])}</h2><p><b>{esc(r["category"])}</b> · {esc(r["owner"])} · {esc(r["status"])}</p><p>{esc(r["summary"])}</p><p><b>Method:</b> {esc(r["methodology"])}</p><ul>'+''.join(f'<li>{esc(c)}</li>' for c in r['caveats'])+f'</ul><p><b>Dated evidence:</b> {esc(r["date"] or "Not established")} · {esc(r["dateLabel"])} · <a href="{esc(r["dateSourceUrl"],quote=True)}">Date source ↗</a></p><p>{links}</p></article>')
end='''<h2>Maintaining this record</h2><p>Edit <a href="data/adoptions.json">data/adoptions.json</a>; one project per related family. Every record needs a primary source, relationship, source-review date, method and caveats. Dates require a separate basis and source URL; use null if unknown. Counts and the chart update from the JSON. Regenerate this report after editing the data. Source verification requires a manual recheck. See README.md for local preview, validation and GitHub Pages instructions. Contribute updates through the <a href="https://github.com/JamesWeatherhead/asq-phi-in-the-wild">website repository</a>, using <a href="https://github.com/JamesWeatherhead/asq-phi-in-the-wild/blob/main/data/adoptions.json">data/adoptions.json</a>.</p><p>Audit status: a broad public-source snapshot with explicit access limits, not an exhaustive systematic review. Recheck mutable URLs and preprint versions before making a public announcement.</p><a class="button" href="index.html">Return to the directory →</a>'''
(root/'audit-report.html').write_text('<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>Audit &amp; sources — ASQ-PHI In the Wild · '+esc(audit_label)+'</title><link rel="stylesheet" href="styles.css"></head><body><main class="report">'+intro+''.join(parts)+end+'</main></body></html>')
